{
 "classification": "frontend screen composition - CPS layer/object structure only; no ROM bytes, no imagery",
 "colour_ram_finding": "LIVE palette banks per frame: character select 17, title/attract 19, round-1 title 32. The Saturn build currently allocates AVSP_EXACT_PALETTE_BANKS = 8 (128 colours) for actors. The frontend therefore needs 2-4x the current colour-RAM allocation and cannot be rendered faithfully inside it. This is the AvP-specific validation of the reference port's warning that a per-tile pipeline spends COLOUR RAM rather than VDP1 texture memory; the reference's own 12-14 live banks per combat anchor is context, never an AvP budget.",
 "finding": "the settled character-select screen is drawn almost entirely by the three CPS tilemap layers; its only drawn objects are the small 1P cursor marker. The plate slide-in is a large transient object burst. The title/attract page uses a DIFFERENT set of tilemap base addresses than the select page, so the two are distinct tilemap pages in gfxram.",
 "implication_for_the_port": "a faithful rebuild needs a CPS tilemap path (tile codes + palette per layer) in addition to the existing per-tile VDP1 object path; it cannot be done with sprites alone, and it does not need a captured picture.",
